been covered up long ago by the deep drifts of snow.  Carried along by the
wind, a howl echoes, followed by a faint wailing that beckons those closer
into the forest.  Lending to a lighter atmosphere, the chirping of snow birds
rings high overhead and from the forest ahead.  Two choices are present,
plunge into the forest or retreat toward the east.
