#38753
"Dense Pine Forest"
"Small piles of snow cover the forest floor like tiny burial mounds.  Impaled
in the snow are dozens of fallen twigs and small branches broken off by the
heavy burden of snow while surrounding them is a blanket of brown and green
pine needles.  The aged pine trees which make up the forest are dark in color
with vibrant green needles, some scarred and damaged from natural hazards. 
Virtually untouched by the rigors of time, the trees have all survived except
those that have collapsed from the snow or broken under the wind's will.  A
medium-sized boulder stands in the center of the grove, alone in its winter
slumber.
"
