north is a wall of jagged gray rock matted in ice and frozen mud.  Slanting
south is a steep cliff, impassible by normal means.  However, it presents a
majestic a view of a dense pine forest gathered around the base of the
mountain.  The scene is like a blanket of pointed green spikes tipped with
ice.  Nestled amongst a shelter of rocks to the west, steam rises from a
rippling pool of warm water.  Squeezing through a pile of large boulders the
path leads down the slope.
