#38759
"Narrow Mountain Pass"
"The wind continues to beat down upon all that attempt to travel through the
steep crags, sapping their reserve of strength.  A bank of snow piles up on
the northern mountain's southern face as more ice and frozen debris is
constantly being blown into the ever-growing mound.  Cradled within the rocks
offset from the trail to the south, a large pool of water sends steam skyward
as it cools in the cold, mountain air.  Vast amounts of heat radiate from the
pool's surface resembling a slow cooking pot.  Beinging within close proximity
to this natural hot spring warms the body, easing the cold, numbing feeling
from the bones.  Parts of the road sheltered from the wind seem clear of deep
snow, allowing it to be followed to the east or west along the contour of the
mountainside.
"
