#38786
"Snowy Plain"
"A jagged glacier about half the size of a mountain lies to the southwest
across the plain of snow.  across the plain of snow.  Gaining in size over
many years, the glacier appears like no one would be able to climb over the
ice.  Instead it leaves the choice of continuing along the snow plain and its
fierce chilly winds and the near zero visibility as snows pound against all in
their way.  Humanoid sized animal tracks cross back and forth across the snow
leaving a trail in all directions.  Most of the tracks appear to be very
recent.
"
