#38790
"Snowy Plain"
"Without mercy, the cold chilly winds beat upon all across the snow plain like
a giant with his club.  The harsh cold climate causes even the bravest and
strongest to buckle slightly against the will of nature.  Appearing lifeless,
the snow plains have all but buried specs of frozen plants beneath the surface
in a deep grave of white ice.  With visibility dimming for moments at a time,
a ice covered mountain to south appears to be impassable.  Instead the
mountain acts like a barrier holding the snow plain in the center of the
mountain range.
"
"steep mountain south
