#38791
"Snowy Plain"
"A black appearing mountain of ice and cold stone to the south stares down
icily upon all those crossing the snow plain.  Lurking near the base of the
mountain is a half-mountain sized glacier of solid jagged ice.  Both these
objects of the cold are impassable and appear more treacherous than the snow
plain.  The wind whips like an ice, cold bee sting, again, and again, and
again.  Small hills of white snow drift across the frozen snow covered ground
and reform just a few feet away.  The snow plain appears to shift its shape
from the constant snow drifts making the ground somewhat new every few hours.
"
"steep mountain south
