#38792
"Snowy Plain"
"With each step, it seems to sink downward, deep into the snow.  Atop this
ground, the snow appears soft unlike the other ground across the snow plain,
making it easy to sink into the clutches of the white ice.  The ground
although very dangerous, appears less dangerous than the constant avalanches
on the slopes of the southern mountain.  Luckily the avalanche fails to cover
this distance.
"
